  "note": "Tide computed by Vigie from a global ocean tide model: not for navigation, and not an official tide table. Heights are relative to the mean sea level of the model, not to the chart datum of a port. Estimated by Vigie from the model's tide at Brest: 100 times the range of each semi-diurnal tide at Brest divided by 6.10 m. Not the official coefficient, which is SHOM's. In France the coefficient is used for the Atlantic, Channel and North Sea coasts, with the value of the high water at Brest; it says nothing of the Mediterranean or of other countries. SHOM's own definition (height of the high water above the mid-tide level, over a unit, times 100) was measured against this one on the tide observed at Brest and did not come closer (ADR 0018); the model's tide is not corrected, so the coefficient inherits the model's error."
